{#
    The Renovo mark, once per page, as an SVG symbol every other place `<use>`s.

    It is the supplied logo — `assets/brand/renovo-logo.png` — traced to a
    single outline and rounded to one decimal place, which is under 2kB of path
    data and stays crisp at every size the shell puts it at: 32px in the rail,
    24px in the top bar, and whatever a zoomed-in browser asks for.

    Only the mark is here, not the wordmark beside it in the source file. The
    wordmark is navy, which is a colour this application does not own — on the
    dark theme it would sit on a near-black page as an unreadable smudge. What
    goes next to the mark in the rail is `instance_name`, which is the operator's
    to choose and is already translated, themed and legible.

    The fill is the brand gradient by way of the tokens, so the mark recolours
    with the theme rather than carrying two baked-in hex codes that would drift
    from the rest of the palette the first time it was re-sampled. The counters
    — the panel behind the bars, the gap under the swoosh — are holes in one
    even-odd path, so the page shows through them and the mark reads on a light
    surface and a dark one without a second copy.

    Sized 0 and positioned out of the flow rather than `display: none`, which
    some browsers take as licence to stop resolving the gradient inside it.
#}
